{
  "analysis": "The output of `find /disk` gives us a list of files on the system:
- `/disk/etc/passwd`, `/disk/etc/crontab`, `/disk/etc/hosts`, `/disk/etc/hostname`, `/disk/etc/os-release`
- `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat`
- `/disk/var/log/messages`, `/disk/var/log/secure`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/error.log`, `/disk/var/log/secure.1.gz`, `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log`, `/disk/var/log/wtmp.csv`, `/disk/var/log/kern.log`
- `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`
- `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`
- `/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz`, `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz`
- `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys`, `/disk/root/.bashrc`
- `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp`, `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar`

Let's examine each of these key files to gather evidence.",
  "plan": "Examine user accounts, cron jobs, ssh authorized_keys, webshell content, logs, and bash histories.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/etc/passwd /disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat /disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys /disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/home/devops/.bash_history /disk/root/.bashrc\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Let's check all log files and binary/cache files:
1. `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`
2. `/disk/var/log/nginx/error.log`
3. `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log`
4. `/disk/var/log/secure`
5. `zcat /disk/var/log/secure.1.gz`
6. `/disk/var/log/messages`
7. `/disk/var/log/wtmp.csv`
8. `/disk/var/log/kern.log`
9. `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`
10. `/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` and `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz`",
  "plan": "Examine the log files and archive contents to uncover details about the attacker's activities, IP address, exfiltration, log wiping, etc.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/var/log/nginx/access.log /disk/var/log/nginx/error.log /disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/var/log/secure /disk/var/log/messages /disk/var/log/wtmp.csv /disk/var/log/kern.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "zcat /disk/var/log/secure.1.gz\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Let's check the contents of all log files more carefully and separately to capture full outputs:
1. `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`
2. `/disk/var/log/nginx/error.log`
3. `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log`
4. `/disk/var/log/secure`
5. `/disk/var/log/wtmp.csv`
6. `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (or check if it's text/binary)
7. inspect `/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` and `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz`",
  "plan": "Inspect access log, tomcat access-exfil log, wiped bin file, and archive contents.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/var/log/nginx/access.log\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "file /disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin /disk/tmp/.cache/*\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tar -tzvf /disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz 2>/dev/null; tar -tzvf /disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Notice that `/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` and `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` are NOT actual tar.gz files!
File command output:
`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz: Unicode text, UTF-8 text`
`/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz: ASCII text`

Let's inspect the contents of `/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz`, `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz`, and `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`!",
  "plan": "Cat the text contents of `/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz`, `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz`, and check strings/head of `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz /disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "strings /disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin | head -n 30\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Let's check the rest of `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` and see if there are any other text/string lines in it, or in other log files.
Also let's check `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log` and any other log files line by line or grep for attacker IP / actions.",
  "plan": "Check full strings of `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, check all of `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log` and search for IP 198.51.100.167 or other IPs across `/disk`.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "strings /disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -rn \"198.51.100.167\" /disk/\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The output of grep reveals key findings:
1. `198.51.100.167` is the true source IP address!
- In `/disk/var/log/secure:213`: `Aug  8 00:56:00 struts-prod-01 sshd[1201]: Accepted password for root from 198.51.100.167 port 51900 ssh2`
- Also in `/disk/var/log/secure:183-212`: Bruteforce SSH attempts from `198.51.100.167`.
- In `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391-393`:
  - `POST /uploads/shell.php`
  - `GET /?x=jndi-ldap-lookup-defanged-to-198.51.100.167-1389`
  - `GET /struts2-showcase/` OGNL-probe
- In `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`:
  - `GET /bulk data exfil via HTTP POST to 198.51.100.167 (defanged endpoint) HTTP/1.1`

Let's check the rest of the log files: `/disk/var/log/secure`, `/disk/var/log/messages`, `/disk/var/log/wtmp.csv` to see line numbers and exact entries.",
  "plan": "Examine line numbers in `/disk/var/log/secure`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`, `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log`, and read all of `/disk/var/log/wtmp.csv`.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/var/log/wtmp.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -n 30 /disk/var/log/secure\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -n 20 /disk/var/log/nginx/access.log\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "All five required files have been written to `/app`:
1. `progress.md`
2. `intrusion-report.md`
3. `vuln-report.md`
4. `baseline-report.md`
5. `remediation-plan.md`

Let's do a sanity check on `/app` to ensure all 5 files exist, are non-empty, and contain backtick-delimited citations.",
  "plan": "Check `ls -la /app` and inspect the file sizes.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /app\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}
